## What the licence above does and does not cover

The MIT grant covers **the code of this port and its documentation**: the
GDScript under `scripts/` and `data/*.gd`, the scene in `scenes/`, the test
suites in `tests/`, `verify.sh`, `export_presets.cfg`, `project.godot`, and
the prose in `README.md` and `docs/`.

It covers **nothing else**, and in particular:

- **SkyRoads itself** — its game design, level layouts, artwork, music,
  sound, palettes, fonts and data files — is copyright **Bluemoon
  Interactive**. It was released as freeware by them and is still distributed
  by them. It is not this project's to license, and no grant here reaches it.

- **Everything under `data/` that was produced from the retail release** is a
  derived asset and inherits that position. That includes, non-exhaustively:
  `data/gfx/` and `data/sprites/` (decoded from the retail `.LZS` archives),
  `data/levels/` and `data/routes/` (from `ROADS.LZS`), `data/music/` (OPL2
  streams from `MUZAX.LZS`, rendered to Ogg Vorbis), `data/audio/` (from
  `SFX.SND` and `INTRO.SND`), `data/palettes/`, `data/hud/`, `data/demo.json`
  (from `DEMO.REC`), `data/tables.json` and `data/skyroads_constants.gd`
  (tables and constants read out of `SKYROADS.EXE`), and the icons in
  `data/branding/`, which are composed from that same artwork.

  A different encoding of someone else's work is still their work. These
  files are included so the port is runnable and reviewable, not because the
  encoding created a new copyright.

- **No retail file is redistributed here.** `SKYROADS.EXE`, `*.LZS`, `*.SND`,
  `*.DAT` and `DEMO.REC` are not in this repository and must not be added to
  it.

If you take the code and drop the derived data, the MIT grant is the whole
story. If you ship the data, you are shipping Bluemoon's work and their terms
are the ones that matter — including for anything sold, bundled with ads, or
published to an app store under the SkyRoads name.

## Third-party

The reverse-engineering notes and the C reference implementation this port was
checked against (`skyroads-port/`, outside this repository) are MIT, copyright
2026 Ammaar Reshi, and carry their own exception for Nuked-OPL3 by Alexey
Khokholov (LGPL-2.1). No code from either is included here; they were used as
a reference and as a measuring instrument.
